[0.000, "o", "Have you tried the x11vnc '-ncache' VNC client-side pixel caching feature yet?\r\n\r\nThe scheme stores pixel data offscreen on the VNC viewer side for faster\r\nretrieval.  It should work with any VNC viewer.  Try it by running:\r\n\r\n    x11vnc -ncache 10 ...\r\n\r\nOne can also add -ncache_cr for smooth 'copyrect' window motion.\r\nMore info: http://www.karlrunge.com/x11vnc/faq.html#faq-client-caching\r\n\r\nWebSocket server settings:\r\n  - Listen on :6080\r\n  - Web server. Web root: /usr/share/novnc\r\n  - No SSL/TLS support (no cert file)\r\n  - proxying from :6080 to localhost:5900\r\n192.168.127.1 - - [11/Aug/2026 16:42:29] 192.168.127.1: Plain non-SSL (ws://) WebSocket connection\r\n192.168.127.1 - - [11/Aug/2026 16:42:29] 192.168.127.1: Path: '/websockify'\r\n"]
